What does this program print?

```php
<?php
function f(): string
{
    try {
        echo "a";
        return "b";
    } finally {
        echo "c";
    }
}
echo f(), "\n";
```

What does this program print?

```php
<?php
try {
    throw new InvalidArgumentException("x");
} catch (LogicException $e) {
    echo "logic\n";
} catch (InvalidArgumentException $e) {
    echo "invalid\n";
}
```

What does this program print?

```php
<?php
try {
    try {
        throw new DomainException("inner");
    } catch (DomainException $e) {
        throw new RuntimeException("outer", previous: $e);
    }
} catch (RuntimeException $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), "/", $e->getPrevious()->getMessage(), "/", get_class($e->getPrevious()), "\n";
}
```

What happens when PHP 8.6 runs this?

```php
function g(): string
{
    try {
        throw new RuntimeException("lost");
    } finally {
        return "finally wins";
    }
}
echo g(), "\n";
```
